                        "sense_id": "4719dcee-9caf-315d-a8be-14f74f4af1f4",
                        "entry_id": "2b3667b2-15a7-313b-a0ad-7f265e25728f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pointed, as a cross, or having a point projected, as a bend; varriated."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aca9f15f-ceba-481a-9640-3a9611599d5f",
                                "sense_id": "4719dcee-9caf-315d-a8be-14f74f4af1f4",
                                "text": "A cross urdé seems to be the same with what we otherwise call chleche, or chlechée. See CHLECHE."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c78266d8-5ed9-43da-8c5f-10f3760af5fa",
                                "sense_id": "4719dcee-9caf-315d-a8be-14f74f4af1f4",
                                "text": "The sacred monogram is engraved on the bowl, the top of the letter I forming a cross urdé."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "67ea4820-9b2e-4b46-b252-14d3817797c7",
                                "sense_id": "4719dcee-9caf-315d-a8be-14f74f4af1f4",
                                "text": "Badge : A Cross-urdé resting on wreath of laurels and oak banded gold."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ad78785-b9a6-4820-8ff0-e66130144a6e",
                                "sense_id": "4719dcee-9caf-315d-a8be-14f74f4af1f4",
                                "text": "The decoration consists of a cross urdé enamelled white with gold edges, resting on a wreath of laurel and oak enamelled green . In the centre, edged with gold, is a circular plaque enamelled crimson bearing the cypher […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f69d61f0-5730-4be7-a98a-85bbcd5ec35b",
                                "sense_id": "4719dcee-9caf-315d-a8be-14f74f4af1f4",
                                "text": "In heraldry, as many as 285 varieties of cross have been recognized, but the twelve in ordinary use, and from which the others are derived, are: (1) The ordinary cross; (2) the cross humetté, or couped; (3) the cross urdé[…]"
                            }
                        ]
